<p>President Trump sharply criticized NATO after a closed-door meeting in Washington with Secretary-General Mark Rutte, saying alliance members &quot;weren&#x27;t there&quot; for the United States during the recent war with Iran and voicing frustration that European allies declined to contribute military forces. Rutte called the meeting &quot;very frank&quot; and said it was meant to ease tensions, but it came as reports said the administration is weighing whether to end U.S. participation in the alliance. The latest clash puts fresh strain on a transatlantic partnership that has lasted nearly eight decades, at a moment when Washington is also asking allies to submit plans within days to help secure the Strait of Hormuz after the Iran conflict and ceasefire efforts. Even so, the fact that Trump and Rutte met directly and kept channels open leaves room for more talks on security commitments, burden-sharing, and the alliance’s future.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ZPyPtjn3gVO8MFUQ5uH1hq9DYMrvpNXJhowbYmmjunQLz5oYPyBl8RfyTHZvwj3SL6WZFJf1n0a3-rCdjisq8MrzoNmDD5d_QvPNqit2b_zNdMN_iv2gL4nUXWqKEE5SnzSELnfL_Rg8XJGtuqxXAwU08ts2Bh12ii88Y1ycOkV0xvyXfqSZgL-PWoVGAJYyhyDiO3lyUSeUMuxX6Og1Zjn0xrQRm_6RYdeasUId7TcFX8B6Krmcr4c' alt='Secretary of State Marco Rubio and NATO Secretary General Mark Rutte on Wednesday, April 8, 2026, in Washington.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>White House linkage: During talks between American and NATO officials at the White House, the US request for Hormuz proposals folded maritime security directly into alliance discussions rather than handling it on a separate track.</li><li>Troop pressure: Reports cited by The Hindu said one punishment option under consideration would shift US troops out of NATO countries seen as unhelpful to the Iran war effort.</li><li>Rutte rebuttal: Rutte said &quot;a large majority of European countries&quot; had met their existing commitments, pushing back on Trump’s broader claim that allies had failed Washington.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: After the meeting, Trump also appeared to renew pressure over Greenland, suggesting his dispute with allies goes beyond burden-sharing for the Iran war. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c05d8j9r5ejo'>BBC</a>)</li><li>Mark Rutte: Rutte described the private session as a conversation between &quot;two good friends,&quot; using personal diplomacy to contain the dispute even as he acknowledged Trump’s disappointment over Iran. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/08/nato-mark-rutte-trump-iran-war'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Trump administration: Officials kept the idea of a NATO exit in public view after the Iran-war dispute instead of tamping it down, increasing pressure on European allies. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/8/trump-administration-says-it-is-mulling-nato-withdrawal-after-iran-war'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>European allies: By refusing to send forces for the Iran campaign, European members drew a line between supporting NATO and joining that specific U.S. war. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/08/white-house-says-trump-will-discuss-possibility-of-leaving-nato_6752238_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/08/white-house-says-trump-will-discuss-possibility-of-leaving-nato_6752238_4.html'>Trump blasts NATO after closed-door meeting with Secretary-General Rutte</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/news-wrap-nato-chief-meets-with-trump-in-bid-to-ease-tensions'>News Wrap: NATO chief meets with Trump in bid to ease tensions</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/9/trump-slams-nato-over-iran-after-meeting-rutte-renews-greenland-threat'>Trump slams NATO over Iran after meeting Rutte, renews Greenland threat</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c05d8j9r5ejo'>Trump c